2026-03-19 11:54:39,078 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 0, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 319, "content": "You are architect_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Select the best standard n8n nodes for one workflow stage using only the candidates provided. Do not invent node types. This release only supports classic workflows with main-only compatible nodes. Treat the provided hard constraints as mandatory, not preferences.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 3079, "content": "Workflow objective: User requested a new workflow for: crea un workflow que vaya cogiendo los correos que recibo ylos clasifique con IA por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: crea un workflow que vaya cogiendo los correos que recibo ylos clasifique con IA por nivel de urgencia\nWorkflow summary: A workflow that continuously collects incoming emails and classifies them by urgency level using AI.\nCurrent stage id: stage1\nCurrent stage name: Collect Incoming Emails\nCurrent stage purpose: Gather all incoming emails from the user's email account in real-time or near-real-time.\nCurrent stage required capabilities: Access to the user's email inbox, Ability to retrieve emails continuously\nCurrent stage expected inputs: Incoming emails (subject, body, sender, timestamp, etc.)\nCurrent stage expected outputs: A stream of raw incoming emails ready for processing\nPrevious selected stages: -\n\nCandidate nodes:\n- Node Type: n8n-nodes-base.cron\n  Display Name: Cron\n  Usage Mode: action_only\n  Usable As Tool: False\n  Has Main Input: False\n  Input Connection Types: -\n  Output Connection Types: main\n  Type Version: 1\n  Capability Summary: Triggers the workflow at a specific time Workflow management in Embed / Workflow per user / 1. Obtain user credentials Here you need to capture all credentials for any node/service this user must authenticate with, along with any additional parameters requir...\n  Limitations: -\n  Hard Reject Reasons In v1: -\n  Evidence Refs: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.scheduletrigger/\n- Node Type: @n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chatTrigger\n  Display Name: Chat Trigger\n  Usage Mode: action_only\n  Usable As Tool: False\n  Has Main Input: False\n  Input Connection Types: -\n  Output Connection Types: main\n  Type Version: 1\n  Capability Summary: Runs the workflow when an n8n generated webchat is submitted Advanced AI / Related resources / Chat trigger Use the [n8n Chat Trigger](/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-langchain.chattrigger/index.md) to trigger a workflow based on chat interactions.\n  Limitations: -\n  Hard Reject Reasons In v1: -\n  Evidence Refs: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-langchain.chattrigger/\n\nRules:\n- Select only from the listed node types.\n- Prefer the smallest bundle that fully satisfies the stage without breaking the overall workflow.\n- Keep the overall workflow coherent from start to finish.\n- For the first stage, only explicit inbound trigger/listener/polling nodes are valid.\n- Send, post, respond, reply, and dispatch nodes are invalid for intake stages.\n- Reject any candidate with hard reject reasons in v1.\n- In v1, reject any node that requires ai_languageModel, ai_tool, ai_memory, or any other non-main required connector.\n- If the stage is heuristic or rule-based, reject AI or LLM classifier nodes unless the user explicitly asked for AI.\n- Stage requires trigger-capable node: True.\n- If no candidate fits confidently, set needs_clarification=true and ask only the minimum question needed.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.1}, "request_id": "1d7af64821", "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_selection", "total_chars": 3398, "ts_utc": "2026-03-19T10:54:39.078776+00:00"}
