2026-03-19 13:59:16,212 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 0, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 437, "content": "You are architect_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Select the best standard n8n nodes for one workflow stage using only the candidates provided. Do not invent node types. This release only supports classic workflows with main-only compatible nodes. Treat the provided hard constraints as mandatory, not preferences. Reason like a workflow architect, not like a semantic search engine: choose nodes by structural role in the workflow.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 3722, "content": "Workflow objective: User requested a new workflow for: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: ### Task: Suggest 3-5 relevant follow-up questions or prompts that the user might naturally ask next in this conversation as a **user**,...\nWorkflow summary: Abstract workflow plan for suggesting relevant follow-up questions or prompts based on chat history to continue or deepen a discussion.\nCurrent stage id: stage1\nCurrent stage name: Analyze Chat History\nCurrent stage purpose: Extract key topics, context, and user intent from the chat history to identify natural follow-up opportunities.\nCurrent stage required capabilities: Understand conversational context, Identify relevant themes or topics in a discussion, Determine user intent or direction of the conversation\nCurrent stage expected inputs: Chat history (transcript or log), Guidelines for generating follow-up questions (e.g., conciseness, relevance, no repetition)\nCurrent stage expected outputs: List of identified key topics or themes, User intent or direction of the conversation, Potential gaps or areas to deepen the discussion\nPrevious selected stages: -\n\nRecent upstream selected nodes and connectors:\n-\n\nCandidate nodes:\n- Node Type: n8n-nodes-base.evaluationTrigger\n  Display Name: Evaluation Trigger\n  Usage Mode: action_only\n  Usable As Tool: False\n  Has Main Input: False\n  Input Connection Types: -\n  Output Connection Types: main\n  Type Version: 1\n  Capability Summary: Run a test dataset through your workflow to check performance Metric-based evaluations / How it works / 2. Add metrics to workflow * **Correctness (AI-based)**: Whether the answer's meaning is consistent with a supplied reference answer. Uses a scale of 1 to 5, with 5 being the...\n  Limitations: -\n  Hard Reject Reasons In v1: -\n  Evidence Refs: n8n://node/n8n-nodes-base.evaluationTrigger\n\nRules:\n- Select only from the listed node types.\n- Prefer the smallest bundle that fully satisfies the stage without breaking the overall workflow.\n- Keep the overall workflow coherent from start to finish.\n- Use the recent upstream selected nodes as hard context for compatibility, I/O continuity, and realistic sequencing.\n- Avoid selecting a node that would make the previous 2 to 3 stages impossible to connect coherently.\n- Decide by functional role, not just semantic similarity. Distinguish trigger, poller, classifier, model provider, transformer, router, and sink roles.\n- Reject provider-only or infrastructure-only nodes when the stage needs a complete business operation node.\n- Prefer nodes whose main inputs and outputs naturally match the stage I/O and the nearest upstream node outputs.\n- If a candidate would require an extra hidden node, hidden model attachment, or hidden auxiliary connection to work, reject it in this selection step.\n- For the first stage, only explicit inbound trigger/listener/polling nodes are valid.\n- Send, post, respond, reply, and dispatch nodes are invalid for intake stages.\n- Reject any candidate with hard reject reasons in v1.\n- In v1, reject any node that requires ai_languageModel, ai_tool, ai_memory, or any other non-main required connector.\n- If the stage is heuristic or rule-based, reject AI or LLM classifier nodes unless the user explicitly asked for AI.\n- Stage requires trigger-capable node: True.\n- Before selecting, perform a private compatibility check against: stage intent, stage I/O, previous 2 to 3 stages, and likely next-stage connectivity.\n- If no candidate fits confidently, set needs_clarification=true and ask only the minimum question needed.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.1}, "request_id": "a88e137aff", "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_selection", "total_chars": 4159, "ts_utc": "2026-03-19T12:59:16.212824+00:00"}
