2026-03-19 14:11:21,036 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"estimated_tokens": 0, "event": "llm_prompt", "message_count": 2, "messages": [{"chars": 437, "content": "You are architect_agent for an n8n workflow assistant. Select the best standard n8n nodes for one workflow stage using only the candidates provided. Do not invent node types. This release only supports classic workflows with main-only compatible nodes. Treat the provided hard constraints as mandatory, not preferences. Reason like a workflow architect, not like a semantic search engine: choose nodes by structural role in the workflow.", "role": "system"}, {"chars": 3360, "content": "Workflow objective: User requested a new workflow for: crea un workflow que vaya cogiendo los correos que recibo ylos clasifique con IA por nivel de urgencia\nDesired outcome: Deliver an abstract workflow plan that satisfies: crea un workflow que vaya cogiendo los correos que recibo ylos clasifique con IA por nivel de urgencia\nWorkflow summary: Abstract workflow plan for receiving emails and classifying them by urgency level using AI.\nCurrent stage id: stage1\nCurrent stage name: Receive Emails\nCurrent stage purpose: Capture incoming emails from the user's email account in real-time or batch mode, depending on the system's capabilities.\nCurrent stage required capabilities: Inbound email processing, Email retrieval (real-time or batch)\nCurrent stage expected inputs: Emails received by the user\nCurrent stage expected outputs: Raw emails with metadata (e.g., sender, subject, body, timestamp, etc.)\nPrevious selected stages: -\n\nRecent upstream selected nodes and connectors:\n-\n\nCandidate nodes:\n- Node Type: n8n-nodes-base.cron\n  Display Name: Cron\n  Usage Mode: action_only\n  Usable As Tool: False\n  Has Main Input: False\n  Input Connection Types: -\n  Output Connection Types: main\n  Type Version: 1\n  Capability Summary: Triggers the workflow at a specific time Workflow management in Embed / Single workflow / Call the workflow For each new user, or for any existing user as may be needed, call the webhook defined as the workflow trigger and provide the necessary credentials (...\n  Limitations: -\n  Hard Reject Reasons In v1: -\n  Evidence Refs: https://docs.n8n.io/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.scheduletrigger/\n\nRules:\n- Select only from the listed node types.\n- Prefer the smallest bundle that fully satisfies the stage without breaking the overall workflow.\n- Keep the overall workflow coherent from start to finish.\n- Use the recent upstream selected nodes as hard context for compatibility, I/O continuity, and realistic sequencing.\n- Avoid selecting a node that would make the previous 2 to 3 stages impossible to connect coherently.\n- Decide by functional role, not just semantic similarity. Distinguish trigger, poller, classifier, model provider, transformer, router, and sink roles.\n- Reject provider-only or infrastructure-only nodes when the stage needs a complete business operation node.\n- Prefer nodes whose main inputs and outputs naturally match the stage I/O and the nearest upstream node outputs.\n- If a candidate would require an extra hidden node, hidden model attachment, or hidden auxiliary connection to work, reject it in this selection step.\n- For the first stage, only explicit inbound trigger/listener/polling nodes are valid.\n- Send, post, respond, reply, and dispatch nodes are invalid for intake stages.\n- Reject any candidate with hard reject reasons in v1.\n- In v1, reject any node that requires ai_languageModel, ai_tool, ai_memory, or any other non-main required connector.\n- If the stage is heuristic or rule-based, reject AI or LLM classifier nodes unless the user explicitly asked for AI.\n- Stage requires trigger-capable node: True.\n- Before selecting, perform a private compatibility check against: stage intent, stage I/O, previous 2 to 3 stages, and likely next-stage connectivity.\n- If no candidate fits confidently, set needs_clarification=true and ask only the minimum question needed.\n", "role": "user"}], "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "params": {"structured": true, "temperature": 0.1}, "request_id": "5784220609", "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_selection", "total_chars": 3797, "ts_utc": "2026-03-19T13:11:21.036493+00:00"}
2026-03-19 14:11:26,386 INFO n8n-assistant.trace: TRACE EVENT {"content_chars": 607, "content_preview": "{\"selected_node_types\":[\"n8n-nodes-base.cron\"],\"rationale\":\"The stage requires a trigger-capable node to receive emails. Among the candidates, 'Cron' is the only one that can act as a trigger (via webhook) and initiate the workflow at specific intervals or in real-time if configured with a short interval. It fits the role of an inbound email processing trigger by calling the workflow's webhook when new emails arrive. No other candidate provides explicit inbound email retrieval capabilities, making 'Cron' the only viable choice for this stage.\",\"needs_clarification\":false,\"clarification_questions\":[]}", "event": "llm_output", "model": "mistralai/ministral-3-14b-reasoning", "request_id": "5784220609", "stage": "multi_agent.architect.stage_selection", "structured": true, "ts_utc": "2026-03-19T13:11:26.386808+00:00"}
